.TH SENSIBLE-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-17" "sensible-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sensible-revamped \- tmux defaults that leave the options you set alone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sensible-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.br
.B sensible-revamped
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ options ]
.B list
.br
.B sensible-revamped resize-sync
.br
.B sensible-revamped doctor
.br
.B sensible-revamped version
.br
.B sensible-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sensible-revamped
sets the defaults most tmux users end up writing by hand: no escape delay, a
large scrollback, windows numbered from 1, truecolor, extended keys and copy
to the system clipboard. Each setting is checked against the running tmux
version and the terminal before it is applied, and an option the person set
is left alone. The entry point
.B sensible-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, and every command goes to tmux in one call.
.PP
The terminal is the one the tmux server started in. tmux gives a plugin its
own TERM and TERM_PROGRAM, so both are read from tmux's global environment.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Set the defaults and bind the keys now. An option is written only while it is
empty or at tmux's own default, a terminal feature or override only when it is
absent, and a key only when it is free.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would run, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B resize\-sync
Turn aggressive-resize off while a control-mode client is attached, keeping
the earlier value in
.BR @sensible_revamped_resize_saved ,
and put it back when the last one leaves. The client hooks run it.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the clipboard tool, infocmp, the keys it
found bound, gum and the core tools. Exits 1 only when a required tool is
missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-keys
or
.BR \-\-reload\-key .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI SENSIBLE_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR SENSIBLE_REVAMPED_KEYS .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B SENSIBLE_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B SENSIBLE_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B SENSIBLE_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B SENSIBLE_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.TP
.BR TERM ,\  TERM_PROGRAM ,\  COLORTERM ,\  LC_TERMINAL
The terminal, which decides truecolor, extended keys, sixel and hyperlinks.
TERM and TERM_PROGRAM come from the environment the tmux server started in.
.TP
.BR EDITOR ,\  VISUAL
vi in either one turns the copy-mode keys to vi.
.TP
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,\  DISPLAY
Decide between wl-copy and the X11 clipboard tools.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default.
.TP
.B @sensible_revamped_keys
off skips C\-p, C\-n, the last\-window key and the reload key. The custom
prefix and the copy\-mode keys still apply. The default is on.
.TP
.B @sensible_revamped_last_window_key
A prefix key that switches to the last window. The default is none.
.TP
.B @sensible_revamped_reload_key
A prefix key that sources the config file again and says so. The default is
none.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The plugin writes one option itself:
.B @sensible_revamped_resize_saved
holds the aggressive-resize value while a control-mode client is attached.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR infocmp (1),
.BR gum (1)
